WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:02.068
[music playing]

00:00:02.101 --> 00:00:03.970
 Mark, Chris, congratulations.

00:00:04.036 --> 00:00:06.472
The strength of your
weapons has carried you

00:00:06.539 --> 00:00:08.541
into the final round
of this competition.

00:00:08.608 --> 00:00:10.376
Now we're sending you
back to your home forges

00:00:10.442 --> 00:00:13.379
to recreate an iconic
weapon from history.

00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:19.152
That weapon is--
the tabar shishpar.

00:00:22.255 --> 00:00:23.622
Good luck, bladesmiths.

00:00:23.689 --> 00:00:25.958
We'll see you in five days.

00:00:25.991 --> 00:00:27.160
 Good luck.

00:00:29.896 --> 00:00:33.065
 I have to build
this tabar shishpar.

00:00:33.132 --> 00:00:35.502
I have never made a
bludgeoning weapon.

00:00:35.568 --> 00:00:38.538
Today I'm going to work on
the shaft of this weapon.

00:00:38.604 --> 00:00:41.374
I have material, but I don't
think it's quite tough enough,

00:00:41.407 --> 00:00:43.143
so I'm going to put
another one inside of it

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:45.744
to make sure that it can
stand any challenge that they

00:00:45.811 --> 00:00:46.979
give me.

00:00:47.046 --> 00:00:48.847
A little bit heavier,
but I think the judges

00:00:48.881 --> 00:00:51.551
are up to that challenge.

00:00:51.617 --> 00:00:54.653
I've forged the handle
areas into my shaft.

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:56.956
The whole shaft is as
straight as I can make it,

00:00:57.023 --> 00:00:58.524
so we'll get ready
to heat treat this.

00:00:58.590 --> 00:01:01.628
I've never quenched
a hollow tube before.

00:01:01.694 --> 00:01:03.196
Kids, don't try this at home.

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:11.871
That was exciting.

00:01:11.938 --> 00:01:14.574
It's like Mount
Vesuvius exploding.

00:01:14.641 --> 00:01:18.144
It's kind of fun to watch
but a little bit scary too.

00:01:18.177 --> 00:01:22.849
There is our hardened
tube of 1084 steel.

00:01:22.915 --> 00:01:25.819
I got a lot of work done,
but I've got a lot of work

00:01:25.885 --> 00:01:26.686
still ahead of me.

00:01:29.589 --> 00:01:31.657 line:0%
 I got all the forging
done, everything

00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:32.925 line:7%
forged into rough shape.

00:01:32.959 --> 00:01:37.763
The first step today is get the
parts of the mace cut to shape.

00:01:37.797 --> 00:01:39.899
So far, so good.

00:01:39.933 --> 00:01:42.168
The five pieces have
to be consistent,

00:01:42.235 --> 00:01:46.172
so when you look at that
mace everything's perfect.

00:01:46.206 --> 00:01:47.906
All in a row.

00:01:47.973 --> 00:01:49.042
Kind of feeling pretty good.

00:01:49.075 --> 00:01:51.544
I'm ahead of schedule.

00:01:51.611 --> 00:01:52.978
Finally done shaping.

00:01:53.045 --> 00:01:55.181
Now it's time to heat treat.

00:01:55.248 --> 00:01:56.582
What could go wrong?

00:01:56.616 --> 00:01:59.151
All the work so far is
coming down to this step.

00:01:59.218 --> 00:02:01.387
If I don't get this right,
the rest of the time

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:03.622
will have been for
nothing, really.

00:02:03.689 --> 00:02:05.391
OK, ax heads going in.

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:16.336
I got the heat treating done.

00:02:16.369 --> 00:02:18.738 line:7%
I couldn't be happier.

00:02:18.771 --> 00:02:20.806 line:0%
 I feel like I'm a
bit ahead of my game.

00:02:20.873 --> 00:02:25.177
Yesterday I forged out my
tabar ax as well as my flanges.

00:02:25.244 --> 00:02:26.879
Today I need to do
all my heat treating,

00:02:26.946 --> 00:02:28.080
and that's really important.

00:02:28.147 --> 00:02:31.484
Grab my wire, and do
all these together.

00:02:31.517 --> 00:02:33.252
And then do the ax,
'cause I want to be

00:02:33.318 --> 00:02:34.921
a little more careful with it.

00:02:34.988 --> 00:02:37.089
I need to focus on
not making mistakes.

00:02:37.156 --> 00:02:41.226
Without the heat treat,
I don't have a weapon.

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:43.062
Despite all the work
I've done, nothing

00:02:43.129 --> 00:02:47.367
matters until this thing comes
out of that oil looking happy.

00:02:52.472 --> 00:02:53.806
It's an ax.

00:02:53.873 --> 00:02:54.974
I'm feeling really good.

00:02:55.007 --> 00:02:56.241
I got my flanges heat treated.

00:02:56.275 --> 00:02:57.543
I got the ax heat treated.

00:02:57.609 --> 00:02:59.412
And tomorrow I can
work on assembly.

00:03:02.048 --> 00:03:05.051 line:0%
 I will be spending a lot
of time on the grinder today.

00:03:05.118 --> 00:03:07.186
It's time to start
grinding things to shape.

00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:10.256
So we're cruising
downhill from here.

00:03:12.925 --> 00:03:14.127
Yeah.

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:16.128
For three days I was
thinking, everything

00:03:16.162 --> 00:03:18.197
is going too darn smooth.

00:03:18.264 --> 00:03:19.598
Something's gonna happen.

00:03:19.665 --> 00:03:21.133
And it did.

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:22.368
I found two cracks.

00:03:22.401 --> 00:03:24.270
Right now, I'm looking
at two options.

00:03:24.337 --> 00:03:26.205
I can try and make
this one work,

00:03:26.272 --> 00:03:27.940
or start over and
make a new one.

00:03:28.007 --> 00:03:29.409
I may be able to
save this blade.

00:03:29.475 --> 00:03:32.211
I'm going to cut this
out right like this.

00:03:32.278 --> 00:03:34.180
I could cut around
the first crack

00:03:34.246 --> 00:03:37.083
and grind out the one on top.

00:03:37.149 --> 00:03:39.051
I'm not taking any
chances with this.

00:03:39.118 --> 00:03:40.553
I don't want to
have it fail on me.

00:03:40.619 --> 00:03:42.822
So I'm going to give
this thing the toughest

00:03:42.889 --> 00:03:43.990
test that I could give it.

00:03:49.462 --> 00:03:52.298
I think it'll be good.

00:03:52.365 --> 00:03:53.700
 Bladesmiths.

00:03:53.766 --> 00:03:57.670
A tabar shishpar is one weapon
with multiple personalities.

00:03:57.737 --> 00:04:00.606
To see what kind of lethal
damage your weapon will do,

00:04:00.672 --> 00:04:02.108
I will take your
tabar shishpar and use

00:04:02.175 --> 00:04:06.379
both hands to deliver killing
blows on this ballistics dummy.

00:04:06.446 --> 00:04:07.813
Mark, you're up first.
You ready?

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:08.781
 Mm-hm.

00:04:08.815 --> 00:04:09.682
Let's see it.

00:04:09.749 --> 00:04:13.319
[music playing]

00:04:27.933 --> 00:04:30.570
 Well, Mark, it is sharp.

00:04:30.636 --> 00:04:35.842
That chopped right into the
chest cavity, breaking a bone.

00:04:35.908 --> 00:04:38.978
This ax dug in and gutted him.

00:04:39.044 --> 00:04:41.747
Your mace definitely will crush.

00:04:41.814 --> 00:04:45.217
You could see the
breaking bones inside.

00:04:45.284 --> 00:04:47.286
Your weapon will kill.

00:04:47.353 --> 00:04:48.287
 Thank you.

00:04:48.353 --> 00:04:49.555
 Chris, you ready?

00:04:49.588 --> 00:04:50.222
 I am.

00:04:50.289 --> 00:04:53.826
[music playing]

00:05:03.736 --> 00:05:05.605
[laughs]

00:05:05.672 --> 00:05:07.273
 Oh, my gosh!

00:05:07.339 --> 00:05:09.509
Into the lung, into the heart.

00:05:09.542 --> 00:05:13.346
Your mace definitely
penetrated through the skull.

00:05:13.412 --> 00:05:15.715
Bones are broken.

00:05:15.781 --> 00:05:17.850
I don't think it's
going to end well.

00:05:17.917 --> 00:05:19.819
Your weapon is heavy.

00:05:19.885 --> 00:05:22.454
And I'm not a fan
of heavy weapons,

00:05:22.521 --> 00:05:24.356
only because you have
to carry it to battle.

00:05:24.423 --> 00:05:27.926
But overall, it will kill.

00:05:27.993 --> 00:05:29.028
 Thank you.

00:05:29.095 --> 00:05:30.929
 All right, gentlemen,
this is the sharpness test.

00:05:30.996 --> 00:05:34.733
The tabar only has one sharp
area, which is the ax head.

00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:37.870
So I'll strike into this
side of beef six times

00:05:37.903 --> 00:05:39.838
with each of your axes.

00:05:39.905 --> 00:05:40.540
Mark, you're up first.

00:05:40.573 --> 00:05:41.273
Are you ready for this?

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:42.241
 Mm-hm.

00:05:42.308 --> 00:05:45.812
[music playing]

00:05:57.223 --> 00:05:57.990
 Ugh!

00:06:02.195 --> 00:06:04.397
Your weapon's nice
and light for a weapon

00:06:04.463 --> 00:06:06.799
that looks as heavy as this is.

00:06:06.866 --> 00:06:11.370
You can see that this just
went right through the ribs.

00:06:11.437 --> 00:06:13.205
This is definitely a cutter.

00:06:13.272 --> 00:06:14.040
Good job.

00:06:14.073 --> 00:06:14.807
 Thank you.

00:06:14.873 --> 00:06:17.076
 Chris, you ready?

00:06:17.143 --> 00:06:18.044
 Let's do it.

00:06:18.111 --> 00:06:21.647
[music playing]

00:06:36.963 --> 00:06:39.899
[laughs]

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:43.602
 Well, right off,
the weight difference.

00:06:43.669 --> 00:06:46.038
I mean, this thing
hits like a ton.

00:06:46.105 --> 00:06:49.808
These hooks tear meat
coming out the back way.

00:06:49.875 --> 00:06:54.447
Your edge-- there's no
damage that I can feel.

00:06:54.514 --> 00:06:59.217
It's heavy, but it does a
hell of a lot of damage.

00:06:59.284 --> 00:07:00.086
Nicely done.

00:07:00.119 --> 00:07:01.153
 Thank you.

00:07:01.187 --> 00:07:02.822
 All right, gentlemen,
this is the strength test.

00:07:02.889 --> 00:07:05.024
Now, to test the strength
and durability of your tabar

00:07:05.057 --> 00:07:08.127
shishpars, I'll be
using all parts of it

00:07:08.193 --> 00:07:10.262
to strike this suit of armor.

00:07:10.329 --> 00:07:11.096
Mark, you're up.

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:11.830
You're ready?

00:07:11.897 --> 00:07:12.398
 Yes, I am.

00:07:12.465 --> 00:07:14.100
Let's see it.

00:07:14.167 --> 00:07:17.703
[music playing]

00:07:33.185 --> 00:07:35.153
 Edge is still perfect.

00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:37.356
No chips, no rolling.

00:07:37.423 --> 00:07:39.558
The hammer gave that
armor a nice dent.

00:07:39.625 --> 00:07:41.360
It didn't take any damage.

00:07:41.426 --> 00:07:43.428
The mace is fine.

00:07:43.495 --> 00:07:45.164
The guy inside
there was not happy.

00:07:45.231 --> 00:07:46.699
 [laughs]

00:07:47.333 --> 00:07:48.133
 All right, Chris.

00:07:48.167 --> 00:07:48.968
You ready for this?

00:07:49.034 --> 00:07:50.002
 Don't hold back.

00:07:50.036 --> 00:07:50.803
 I'm not gonna.

00:07:56.341 --> 00:07:59.879
[music playing]

00:08:15.695 --> 00:08:17.295
This is a heavy weapon.

00:08:17.362 --> 00:08:18.664
 Yeah.

00:08:18.731 --> 00:08:22.668
 I mean, I can control it,
but I don't have any rebound.

00:08:22.702 --> 00:08:27.740
And you got just the smallest
bit of edge deformation here.

00:08:27.806 --> 00:08:31.510
Other than that, the
mace is a devastator.

00:08:31.577 --> 00:08:33.378
You made a beautiful piece.

00:08:33.445 --> 00:08:34.713
 Thank you.

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:36.715 line:0%
I hope the judges appreciate
the devastation my weapon's

00:08:36.749 --> 00:08:38.283 line:7%
capable of bringing.

00:08:38.350 --> 00:08:41.153
It's hard to say
who's going to win.

00:08:41.219 --> 00:08:44.557
 Bladesmiths, the judges'
deliberation is complete,

00:08:44.624 --> 00:08:47.693
and there can only be one
Forged in Fire champion.

00:08:47.760 --> 00:08:49.128
And that champion is--

00:08:52.732 --> 00:08:53.765
Mark.

00:08:53.832 --> 00:08:56.335
Congratulations, you are
the Forged in Fire champion.

00:08:56.368 --> 00:08:58.237
 Thank you.

00:08:58.304 --> 00:08:59.472
Good job, buddy.

00:08:59.505 --> 00:09:00.606
 Thanks.

00:09:00.639 --> 00:09:03.208
 Chris, your blade
did not make the cut.

00:09:03.242 --> 00:09:04.476
David Baker will explain.

00:09:04.543 --> 00:09:05.878
 Chris, Doug and
I both agree that

00:09:05.945 --> 00:09:08.480
the extreme weight
of your weapon

00:09:08.513 --> 00:09:09.948
made it difficult to control.

00:09:10.015 --> 00:09:12.584
And, frankly, I'm still
feeling it in my arm.

00:09:12.651 --> 00:09:14.186
That combined with
that minor edge damage

00:09:14.253 --> 00:09:16.621
you took in the strength
test, those are the reasons

00:09:16.688 --> 00:09:18.156
we're letting you go.

00:09:18.223 --> 00:09:19.224
 Understood.

00:09:19.291 --> 00:09:20.893
 Chris, it's that time.

00:09:20.926 --> 00:09:22.228
Please surrender your weapon.

00:09:26.432 --> 00:09:27.967
 [yells]

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:30.503
[laughs]

00:09:30.536 --> 00:09:31.237
I just--

00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:36.008
[sighs]

00:09:36.075 --> 00:09:39.278
I think I put up the best I
was capable of in the time

00:09:39.344 --> 00:09:40.245
that I was given.

00:09:40.312 --> 00:09:41.246
 See you later, buddy.

00:09:41.313 --> 00:09:42.682
 It's been a pleasure.

00:09:42.748 --> 00:09:45.851
Mark did good work, and his
was just a little bit better.

00:09:49.422 --> 00:09:50.789
 Mark, congratulations.

00:09:50.823 --> 00:09:52.691
You are the Forged
in Fire champion

00:09:52.757 --> 00:09:54.893
and will be receiving
a check for $10,000.

00:09:54.960 --> 00:09:55.460
Good job.

00:09:55.527 --> 00:09:58.864
[applause]

00:10:00.132 --> 00:10:01.433
How do you feel right now?

00:10:01.500 --> 00:10:02.568
 I feel great.

00:10:02.634 --> 00:10:04.736
Chris, a hell of an opponent.

00:10:04.803 --> 00:10:06.472
I'm glad it went
to the very end.

00:10:06.538 --> 00:10:08.874
I wanted to see a
real competition.

00:10:08.941 --> 00:10:11.744
 Mark, please present
your weapon to the judges

00:10:11.811 --> 00:10:13.279
and shake our hands.

00:10:13.312 --> 00:10:14.046
 I won.

00:10:14.112 --> 00:10:15.413
I am the champion.

00:10:15.480 --> 00:10:17.383
Phew.

00:10:17.450 --> 00:10:18.683
Unbelievable.

00:10:18.717 --> 00:10:20.653
I just won $10,000.

00:10:20.719 --> 00:10:22.554
My wife and I, we made a deal.

00:10:22.587 --> 00:10:26.258
She gets 9,000, and I get 1,000.

00:10:26.325 --> 00:10:28.560
So congratulations, dear.

00:10:28.594 --> 00:10:31.964
[music playing]

